## 21. Audit Traceability

Every result is traceable to its inputs, assumptions, and engine version.

```text
Audit
 │
 ├── Input Data
 │
 ├── Assumptions
 │
 ├── Calculation Version
 │
 ├── Calculation Result
 │
 ├── Selected Components
 │
 └── Validation Status
```

A calculation result retains its inputs and outputs so a report can be reproduced exactly, even after the engine evolves.

---

## 22. Calculation Result Format

```json
{
  "calculationType": "solar-sizing",
  "status": "valid",
  "inputs": {},
  "assumptions": {},
  "calculations": {},
  "result": {},
  "warnings": [],
  "errors": []
}
```

The implementation uses TypeScript types (or equivalent schemas) to enforce this shape at compile time.

---

## 23. Units

Engineering units are explicit and enforced in the engine layer.

| Quantity | Unit |
|---|---|
| Voltage | V |
| Current | A |
| Power | W |
| Energy | Wh / kWh |
| Resistance | Ω |
| Length | m |
| Area | mm² |
| Frequency | Hz |
| Capacity | Ah |
| Temperature | °C |

Unit conversion happens in the engineering layer — **never** hidden inside UI components.

---

## 24. Design Margins

Margins are explicit and named.

```text
Load design margin
Battery sizing margin
PV sizing margin
Cable sizing margin
Protection margin
Thermal margin
Inverter surge margin
```

A calculation always distinguishes:

```text
Calculated value
Design value
Selected component
```

**Example:**

```text
Calculated PV requirement:  3.42 kW
Design requirement:         4.28 kW
Selected PV array:          4.40 kW
```

